  "solution": "<p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, option A is less than 3. The convergent geometric sum in B is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>Rationalising C gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></math>, while D is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></math>. Therefore D exceeds C, since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></math>, and also exceeds 3.</p><p>Option E is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></math>, since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></math>. To compare E with D, both are positive, so compare squares: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></math> because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></math> (their squares are 36 and 32). Hence D exceeds every other option. Answer D.</p>",
